This extension adds Like a Dragon: Pirate Yakuza in Hawaii modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Shin Ryu Mod Manager will be installed automatically.[/summary]

[size=3][b]This extension will automatically download and install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/743]Shin Ryu Mod Manager[/url]﻿ (SRMM).
[size=3][b][color=#ffff00]You need to enable mods in SRMM to install them to the game files! [/color][color=#b6d7a8]A notification will be shown after deploying mods with a button to run SRMM.[/color][/b][/size][/b][/size]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Steam Demo[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Shin Ryu MM mods with a "shinryumodmanager.exe" file install to the "runtime\media" folder.[/*]
[*]SRMM mods with a "mod-meta.yaml" or "modinfo.ini" file install to the "runtime\media\mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries / Root Folder mods with a "nvngx_dlss.dll" file or a ".exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Data File mods with a ".par" file install to the "runtime\media\data" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/818] [/url]SRMM. You must run SRMM to install mods into the game data archives.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Like a Dragon: Pirate Yakuza in Hawaii mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Shin Ryu MM:

Recognised when the archive contains a "shinryumodmanager.exe" file.

  Installs to: "runtime\media"

========================================================================

SRMM Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "mod-meta.yaml" or "modinfo.ini" file.

  Installs to: "runtime\media\mods"

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "nvngx_dlss.dll", "dstoragecore.dll", "dstorage.dll", "amd_fidelityfx_dx12.dll", "amd_ags_x64.dll" or "libxess.dll".
    - Recognised by any file with the ".exe" extension.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

.par Data File:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".par" file.

  Installs to: "runtime\media\data"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
